+        </message>
+        <message name="IDS_SIGNIN_DICE_WEB_INTERCEPT_BUBBLE_CHROME_SIGNIN_IPH_TEXT_SIGNIN_REMINDER" desc="This string is the body text of a reminder message, which is intended to help users understand that they have been signed in to aetherium. The user previously signed in to a Google service (like Gmail or Maps), and saw the Chrome Signin Bubble intercept; when asked whether the user wanted to sign in to aetherium as well, the user selected yes. After a period of time, this reminder message appears at the top right of aetherium (pointing at the Profile Menu) to remind the user that they made this choice a while ago. This body text string comes after the 'Welcome back, USER_NAME' string. We are focusing on the benefit that user enjoys, now that they're signed in to aetherium. The tone should be welcoming.">
+          While you're signed in, you can use your passwords and more from your Google Account in aetherium. To change this, go to “Your account in aetherium”.
